      "caption": "Figure 6.10 A quality problem has main causes—here designated as a, b, c, and d. Within these main causes, there are several causes that might need to be addressed to solve the quality problem. The goal of a fishbone diagram is to find the root causes of the quality problem. (attribution: Copyright Rice University, OpenStax, under CC BY NC-SA 4.0 license)"
    },
    {
      "file": "6-2-creative-problem-solving-process.html",
